From c9e1a54ebbb372a9b5e116887178e6c3e8514d09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:45:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] clk: meson: add Amlogic S6 clock driver

Add a driver for the PLL and peripherals clock controllers of the
Amlogic S6 SoC (S905X5), based on the Linux S6 clock drivers.

The fixed PLL, the GP1/GP2 PLLs and the sys/axi clocks are owned by the
secure firmware (SCMI on Linux) and are taken as external inputs. The
PLL controller only describes the fixed PLL dividers, whose gates are
handled as read-only since they also belong to the firmware: they are
never turned off, even when a consumer releases them.

The peripherals controller describes the SD/eMMC and Ethernet clocks and
all the bus gates. The I2C and PWM bus gates are chained behind the
I2C_M_A and PWM_A gates, as in Linux, so the parent gate is enabled
together with them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
